# puppet — real-world examples

## Modules

```sh
# List puppet modules loaded
puppet module list

# Install a module from the Forge
puppet module install puppetlabs-ntp
```

## Inspect resources

```sh
# Show current state of all services as Puppet sees them
puppet resource service

# Show one resource (great for generating manifest snippets)
puppet resource service sshd
puppet resource user david
```

## Documentation

```sh
# List describable resource types
puppet describe -l

# Describe one type in detail
puppet describe service | less
```

## Agent runs

```sh
# Re-enable a disabled agent
puppet agent --enable

# One-off verbose test run against the Puppet master
puppet agent -t -v

# Dry run: show what WOULD change
puppet agent -t --noop
```

## Homelab examples

```sh
# Apply a standalone manifest locally (no master needed)
puppet apply ~/puppet/manifests/mediaserver.pp

# Validate a manifest before committing
puppet parser validate ~/puppet/manifests/homelab.pp

# Ensure a package/service pair on Tumbleweed from the CLI
puppet resource package chrony ensure=installed
puppet resource service chronyd ensure=running enable=true
```

## Flag reference

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-t` | Test mode: onetime, verbose, no-daemonize |
| `-v` | Verbose |
| `--noop` | Dry run, report changes only |
| `--enable` / `--disable` | Allow / block agent runs |
